rachel: opened a small docs PR to improve the air-gapped installer UX and expand the KMS/HSM troubleshooting appendix. PR: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/2764. Changes include: clearer cert chain import steps, a Node.js SDK snippet for private endpoints, a short PowerShell conn-check example for ARM64 Windows, and fixing a moved anchor to the bundle verification page. Looking for quick reviews and a security check.

sam: Nice. Can you paste the Node snippet and the PowerShell example here so we can sanity-check flags and TLS verify usage?

rachel: Pasting snippets from the PR:

```powershell
# conn-checker (Windows ARM64 copy/paste)
.\\conn-checker.exe --host 10.0.9.8 --port 8443 --timeout 10 --use-sni --ca C:\\certs\\redwood-ca.pem
```

```js
// Node minimal private endpoint example
const https = require('https');
const payload = JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'hi' });
const options = {
  hostname: '10.0.9.8',
  port: 8443,
  path: '/v1/generate',
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  ca: require('fs').readFileSync('/etc/ssl/redwood-ca.pem')
};
const req = https.request(options, (res) => {
  res.on('data', () => {});
  res.on('end', () => console.log('ok'));
});
req.on('error', (e) => console.error(e));
req.write(payload);
req.end();
```

rachel: Also added a cert import section for Windows and Linux:

- Windows (copy/paste): `certutil -addstore -f \"ROOT\" C:\\certs\\redwood-ca.pem`
- Linux: `sudo cp redwood-ca.pem /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/ && sudo update-ca-certificates`

rachel: For HSM troubleshooting I added: verify NTP (<5s skew), re-import chain after rotation, check PKCS#11 slot numbering (some appliances renumber after firmware updates), and ensure any gateway NAT has hairpin reflection or SNAT for sealed sites.

docs-bot: Linkcheck: PR #2764 -> 1 moved anchor detected: /install/offline-bundle -> /install/airgap/bundle-verify. Suggested replacement applied. Labels: doc:link-fix.

sam: LGTM. Two small nits: 1) in prose use forward-slash paths for readability but include literal Windows escapes in code blocks; 2) add a short security callout in the HSM config sample: never hardcode pins, use env vars or a secret manager.

security: Quick note from compliance: add a reminder to rotate keys off-host before rotation window and to record HSM serials in the rotation playbook. Also say \"do not ship HSM provisioning scripts with production PINs.\"

tina: I fixed the anchor in my follow-up commit and added the security callout. I also swapped the example PKCS11 entry to use `pin = ${HSM_PIN}` to show env var usage.

sam: Approving from docs side. One extra suggestion: include a one-liner showing how to verify both bundle and manifest checksums together: `sha256sum redwood-offline.tar.gz redwood-offline-manifest.json`.

rachel: Added the sha256 example and a short GPG verification note for externally mirrored bundles. Plan: merge on green and add a changelog entry. I'll follow up with a docs ticket to expand the HSM appendix into a dedicated troubleshooting page next sprint. :shipit:

(overview: PR coordination, link fixes, Windows/ARM conn-check snippet, Node SDK example, cert import steps, HSM troubleshooting notes and security callouts)
